# Agent Context Template for Firmware Analysis

This template provides project-specific context for AI agents analyzing firmware issues. Copy it to `AGENT.md` at the root of your firmware repository and replace every placeholder with details from your project.

Avoid putting secrets, customer data, private keys, or credentials in this file.

## Project Overview

- **Product or system**: [Short description of the product, device, or embedded system]
- **Firmware role**: [Bootloader, application firmware, connectivity processor, sensor controller, etc.]
- **Target hardware**: [MCU/SoC family, board name, important peripherals]
- **Operating model**: [RTOS, bare metal, Linux userspace helper, multicore architecture, etc.]
- **Primary languages**: [C, C++, Rust, assembly, Python tooling, etc.]
- **Build system**: [CMake, Make, Bazel, west, vendor IDE, custom scripts, etc.]
- **Supported configurations**: [Board variants, feature flags, build profiles, product SKUs]

